1
00:00:00,541 --> 00:00:04,583
Dear Uncle Napoleon Episode 2

2
00:00:05,291 --> 00:00:10,250
Based on the novel Dear Uncle Napoleon Written by Iraj Pezeshkzad

3
00:00:14,583 --> 00:00:18,208
(Sound of horses galloping)

4
00:00:20,125 --> 00:00:22,125
(Sound of gunfire and warriors shouting)

5
00:00:22,125 --> 00:00:24,125
Subtitles: Iman Soleimani Zadeh

6
00:01:17,041 --> 00:01:20,291
♪ Ride of the valkyrie ♪

7
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:15,833
(Sound of crickets and a dog barking)

8
00:02:28,833 --> 00:02:30,458
Help! - Help!

9
00:02:30,500 --> 00:02:31,583
- Help us!

10
00:02:31,583 --> 00:02:32,666
- Help us!

11
00:02:32,666 --> 00:02:33,666
- A thief!

12
00:02:33,666 --> 00:02:35,083
- Help us!

13
00:02:35,125 --> 00:02:36,958
- Thief! - A thief came!

14
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:39,583
- A thief came, help us!

15
00:02:39,625 --> 00:02:40,625
- Help us!

16
00:02:40,625 --> 00:02:42,458
(Sound of crying) - A thief came

17
00:02:42,500 --> 00:02:44,500
Agha Joon, what’s all this noise? - Help, thief!

18
00:02:45,583 --> 00:02:47,541
Help us! - Thief!

19
00:02:47,541 --> 00:02:48,750
It’s coming from that side, I think!

20
00:02:48,750 --> 00:02:49,750
Let’s go see! (Sound of crying)

21
00:02:49,791 --> 00:02:50,583
Help!

22
00:02:50,625 --> 00:02:52,791
What on earth are we going to do now!

23
00:02:52,791 --> 00:02:54,541
For God’s sake, help us! - A thief came!

24
00:02:54,541 --> 00:02:56,541
Help us, people!

25
00:02:56,541 --> 00:02:58,208
A thief came!

26
00:02:58,250 --> 00:02:59,583
Daddy!

27
00:02:59,625 --> 00:03:02,500
Help, a thief came, help us! - They stole my daddy!

28
00:03:02,500 --> 00:03:03,666
(Sound of crying)

29
00:03:03,666 --> 00:03:05,125
Help, thief!

30
00:03:05,166 --> 00:03:05,708
Help, a thief came!

31
00:03:05,708 --> 00:03:06,708
What’s going on? What’s all the noise?

32
00:03:06,708 --> 00:03:07,791
What happened?

33
00:03:07,833 --> 00:03:09,625
What happened? What’s wrong with Leili? - What’s the matter? Why are you shouting?

34
00:03:09,625 --> 00:03:11,041
Why all the screaming? - They kidnapped Sir!

35
00:03:11,083 --> 00:03:11,750
Th… thief!

36
00:03:11,791 --> 00:03:12,958
Th… th… th…!

37
00:03:12,958 --> 00:03:14,125
He says a thief came! - Help, thief!

38
00:03:14,166 --> 00:03:15,708
Help, thief! - What’s going on here?

39
00:03:15,708 --> 00:03:17,916
A thief came! A thief came! - Why are you making such a fuss!

40
00:03:17,958 --> 00:03:28,791
(Crowd murmurs)

41
00:03:28,833 --> 00:03:30,291
Help us!

42
00:03:30,291 --> 00:03:31,291
He must be in the building right now!

43
00:03:31,333 --> 00:03:33,625
Yes, yes… Colonel… you… search over there.

44
00:03:33,666 --> 00:03:35,416
Yes, yes (Sound of crying)

45
00:03:35,458 --> 00:03:36,291
Help, thief!

46
00:03:36,333 --> 00:03:38,541
Thief be damned… go search over there, quick!

47
00:03:38,583 --> 00:03:39,333
He wasn’t here!

48
00:03:39,375 --> 00:03:40,500
Sir!

49
00:03:40,500 --> 00:03:42,083
Sir! - Check the end of the corridor

50
00:03:42,083 --> 00:03:43,375
Where are you, Sir!

51
00:03:43,416 --> 00:03:44,958
What’s happening? What’s all the noise? - Sir has vanished!

52
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:47,000
Oh, good Lord!

53
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:49,708
Like Sir turned to smoke and rose up to the sky!

54
00:03:49,750 --> 00:03:50,916
Where was he? Where was he sleeping?

55
00:03:50,916 --> 00:03:51,875
In the mosquito net in the yard.

56
00:03:51,916 --> 00:03:53,125
Oh, good Lord!

57
00:03:53,125 --> 00:03:57,250
(Sound of crying and shouting) - Find my dad!

58
00:03:57,250 --> 00:04:00,458
(Sound of crying and shouting) - They stole my dad! You tell me not to cry?

59
00:04:00,500 --> 00:04:02,541
(Sound of crying and shouting) - Which thief would steal Sir?

60
00:04:02,583 --> 00:04:05,041
(Sound of crying and shouting)

61
00:04:05,041 --> 00:04:07,875
(Sound of crying and shouting) - They took Sir… they stole my dad!

62
00:04:11,708 --> 00:04:12,208
Th… th (He stutters)

63
00:04:12,208 --> 00:04:14,583
Th… th… th… th… thief! Help, thief!

64
00:04:14,583 --> 00:04:16,291
Thief… thief… thief

65
00:04:16,333 --> 00:04:17,750
(His voice shakes)

66
00:04:17,791 --> 00:04:19,583
Sir, what are you doing under the bed?!

67
00:04:21,291 --> 00:04:23,708
Help thief, thief, thief, thief… - Sir!

68
00:04:23,750 --> 00:04:25,166
Where are you, Sir!

69
00:04:25,166 --> 00:04:26,708
Ugh… what’s all this wailing?

70
00:04:26,708 --> 00:04:27,958
Here he is, my dear!

71
00:04:27,958 --> 00:04:29,291
Th… th… th… th… th… (He stutters)

72
00:04:29,333 --> 00:04:30,166
Th… th… th… thief!

73
00:04:30,208 --> 00:04:31,000
Thief! Thief!

74
00:04:31,041 --> 00:04:32,375
Thief!… thief!

75
00:04:32,375 --> 00:04:34,500
Seems a snake bit Sir! - Th… th… th…!

76
00:04:34,541 --> 00:04:36,000
Snake what? Why are you talking nonsense?

77
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:38,833
Honestly, Sir, we had a fellow villager, - Th… th… th… thief!

78
00:04:38,875 --> 00:04:39,916
Ah, alright… alright

79
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:41,416
Tell the Colonel to come here.

80
00:04:41,458 --> 00:04:42,750
Honestly, Sir, why should I lie! - Th… th… th…

81
00:04:42,791 --> 00:04:44,000
Mr. Colonel can’t come.

82
00:04:44,041 --> 00:04:46,208
Can’t what? Run and tell him to come here! - Agha Joon!

83
00:04:47,166 --> 00:04:47,583
Agha Joon!

84
00:04:47,625 --> 00:04:48,916
Dear Uncle Colonel fainted from fear of the thief,

85
00:04:48,916 --> 00:04:50,500
In that room! - Th… th… thief… thief… thief!

86
00:04:50,541 --> 00:04:51,083
Thief!

87
00:04:51,458 --> 00:04:52,291
Thief!

88
00:04:52,333 --> 00:04:53,458
Th… th… th… th…

89
00:04:53,458 --> 00:04:55,458
Dear Uncle, why did you go under there!

90
00:04:55,500 --> 00:04:57,500
Why are you frozen? Do something!

91
00:04:57,541 --> 00:05:00,291
Go tell them Sir has been found and stop all this shouting.

92
00:05:00,291 --> 00:05:01,000
Yes, sir!

93
00:05:01,041 --> 00:05:02,541
Saeid… go get Doctor Naser Al-hokama,

94
00:05:02,583 --> 00:05:04,291
Tell him Sir has taken ill, and to come quickly.

95
00:05:04,291 --> 00:05:05,666
No! Don’t go!

96
00:05:05,708 --> 00:05:07,208
I’d rather die

97
00:05:07,250 --> 00:05:10,250
Than see the face of that treacherous lying doctor!

98
00:05:10,250 --> 00:05:11,666
I don’t want to see him!

99
00:05:11,708 --> 00:05:13,125
But why! Are you joking?

100
00:05:13,166 --> 00:05:15,750
That scoundrel can’t keep his mouth shut,

101
00:05:15,791 --> 00:05:17,625
He’ll make a big deal of it!

102
00:05:17,666 --> 00:05:19,166
He’ll embellish it a thousand ways.

103
00:05:19,541 --> 00:05:21,291
It wouldn’t hurt to let him examine you.

104
00:05:21,333 --> 00:05:23,333
No! No! I don’t want to see him!

105
00:05:23,333 --> 00:05:24,375
What kind of talk is this? - Where? Where is he?

106
00:05:24,916 --> 00:05:25,916
Where is he?

107
00:05:28,500 --> 00:05:29,708
What happened to Brother Khan?

108
00:05:30,041 --> 00:05:31,208
Why did you go under the bed?

109
00:05:31,416 --> 00:05:32,833
Was it really a thief?

110
00:05:32,916 --> 00:05:34,625
We saw him with our own eyes!

111
00:05:34,666 --> 00:05:36,333
It’s nothing, please go… - Daddy…

112
00:05:36,333 --> 00:05:37,791
Sir just had a little fright.

113
00:05:37,791 --> 00:05:38,458
Come in, Sir!

114
00:05:38,458 --> 00:05:39,500
Come in!

115
00:05:39,500 --> 00:05:40,000
- Daddy…

116
00:05:40,041 --> 00:05:41,958
You think news of the conspiracy at my brother’s house,

117
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:43,125
Hasn’t reached me?

118
00:05:43,166 --> 00:05:45,541
You’re mistaken, Sir, what conspiracy!

119
00:05:45,583 --> 00:05:46,833
My brother’s house!

120
00:05:46,875 --> 00:05:48,541
For God’s sake, don’t upset yourself…

121
00:05:48,541 --> 00:05:49,458
What conspiracy?

122
00:05:49,625 --> 00:05:51,291
It’s not good for your heart!

123
00:05:51,333 --> 00:05:53,166
My heart is no one’s business!

124
00:05:53,416 --> 00:05:55,125
Just like that night,

125
00:05:55,166 --> 00:05:56,083
That sound,

126
00:05:56,125 --> 00:05:58,458
Had nothing to do with Ghamar’s gas!

127
00:05:58,500 --> 00:05:59,500
You said that?

128
00:05:59,500 --> 00:06:02,041
You think you can fool me?

129
00:06:02,083 --> 00:06:03,125
Not at all, Sir!

130
00:06:03,125 --> 00:06:05,666
I don’t make mistakes, Mr. Doctor!

131
00:06:05,666 --> 00:06:06,958
Go on!

132
00:06:07,458 --> 00:06:09,250
I’m perfectly fine anyway…

133
00:06:09,291 --> 00:06:11,083
And I don’t need your help either!

134
00:06:11,708 --> 00:06:13,291
Go and lie some more,

135
00:06:13,333 --> 00:06:14,833
Hatch another conspiracy!

136
00:06:14,833 --> 00:06:15,750
Ghasem!

137
00:06:15,791 --> 00:06:16,458
Yes, Sir!

138
00:06:16,500 --> 00:06:19,250
What are these people doing in my house?

139
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:22,791
What is my house, an inn?!

140
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:24,291
Throw them out!

141
00:06:24,458 --> 00:06:26,041
Why are you gaping?

142
00:06:26,083 --> 00:06:28,333
I said throw them out!

143
00:06:28,500 --> 00:06:29,375
come on!

144
00:06:29,416 --> 00:06:30,708
All of you out.

145
00:06:30,916 --> 00:06:32,041
You too, kid, out.

146
00:06:32,041 --> 00:06:33,375
But Brother Khan! - Mash Ghasem, me?

147
00:06:34,041 --> 00:06:35,791
Get up, you’ve raised the roof!

148
00:06:35,833 --> 00:06:37,250
He likes this too! Come on… come on…

149
00:06:37,291 --> 00:06:40,000
Come on, go outside… come on, deheee, come on, get moving …. (The old woman is shouting and screaming)

150
00:06:40,041 --> 00:06:41,291
- I won’t go… let go of me!

151
00:06:41,291 --> 00:06:42,083
Brother Khan!

152
00:06:42,125 --> 00:06:43,541
I’d give my life for you.

153
00:06:44,125 --> 00:06:45,666
It’s our own fault anyway,

154
00:06:45,708 --> 00:06:47,750
For giving up a good night’s sleep.

155
00:06:47,791 --> 00:06:49,500
Hero of the Kazerun war,

156
00:06:49,541 --> 00:06:52,333
Having a stroke under the bed over a thief! Heh…

157
00:06:52,333 --> 00:06:52,750
Ghasem…

158
00:06:52,750 --> 00:06:54,250
Give that rifle to me!

159
00:06:54,250 --> 00:06:56,458
I’ll wipe out your whole family!

160
00:06:56,458 --> 00:06:59,291
There’s no place for traitors in my house! - Agha Joon… Agha Joon!

161
00:06:59,291 --> 00:07:02,041
Who let him in here anyway! - It’s all that snitch Poori Feshfeshoo’s fault!

162
00:07:02,041 --> 00:07:03,041
Let him get lost!

163
00:07:03,125 --> 00:07:03,791
Come!

164
00:07:03,916 --> 00:07:04,750
Feshfeshoo!

165
00:07:15,958 --> 00:07:18,416
Waaaaa….. thief!

166
00:07:18,583 --> 00:07:20,041
Th… thth… thththief

167
00:07:20,083 --> 00:07:22,083
Thief came to your house? Thief!-

168
00:07:22,291 --> 00:07:24,541
Th… th…. thii…. thiiii…. thithithithief

169
00:07:24,583 --> 00:07:25,416
Where? Where is he?

170
00:07:25,458 --> 00:07:26,375
There he is! There he is!

171
00:07:26,416 --> 00:07:27,958
Babam Hey!

172
00:07:28,916 --> 00:07:32,041
Hey! It’s Shir-Ali the butcher!

173
00:07:32,041 --> 00:07:32,750
Yes.

174
00:07:32,791 --> 00:07:34,041
It’s us.

175
00:07:34,083 --> 00:07:35,166
Don’t panic!

176
00:07:35,166 --> 00:07:37,000
A thief came to your house?

177
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:39,416
We saw his shadow with our own eyes!

178
00:07:39,458 --> 00:07:40,625
Did he take anything?

179
00:07:41,250 --> 00:07:43,083
Honestly, why should I lie!

180
00:07:43,083 --> 00:07:45,750
We… we didn’t see him take anything with our own eyes!

181
00:07:45,750 --> 00:07:47,833
He came toward us and hid,

182
00:07:47,833 --> 00:07:49,250
We caught him too!

183
00:07:50,291 --> 00:07:52,708
Some fiend got onto our roof!

184
00:07:52,875 --> 00:07:55,500
(The thief with mouth closed tries to speak)

185
00:07:55,541 --> 00:07:56,125
Agha Jan,

186
00:07:56,166 --> 00:07:57,875
Weren’t you well off as you were?!

187
00:07:57,916 --> 00:07:59,416
So why on earth did you steal?

188
00:07:59,458 --> 00:08:04,250
(The thief with mouth closed tries to speak)

189
00:08:04,291 --> 00:08:06,666
Ugh! Ugh! Ugh! Ugh! Ugh! Ugh! Hamdollah!

190
00:08:06,708 --> 00:08:09,000
Why, it’s our own Hamdollah!

191
00:08:09,083 --> 00:08:10,916
Hamdollah!

192
00:08:10,958 --> 00:08:12,750
Hamdollah!

193
00:08:12,791 --> 00:08:15,833
Weren’t you the Doctor’s servant!

194
00:08:16,333 --> 00:08:18,458
Since when are you a thief!

195
00:08:19,166 --> 00:08:20,583
Shir-Ali is tempted

196
00:08:20,625 --> 00:08:22,416
To club him on the head,

197
00:08:22,458 --> 00:08:23,500
And split him in two!

198
00:08:23,500 --> 00:08:25,333
No! Don’t hit, Shir-Ali!

199
00:08:25,833 --> 00:08:27,375
Then what should we do with him, Sir?!

200
00:08:27,958 --> 00:08:30,000
Sir, if you ask us…

201
00:08:30,041 --> 00:08:31,375
Hand him over to the police,

202
00:08:31,416 --> 00:08:32,583
So we can rest easy!

203
00:08:32,750 --> 00:08:34,750
Give him to the police?

204
00:08:35,541 --> 00:08:38,541
Until I get his confession,

205
00:08:38,583 --> 00:08:39,833
I won’t let him go!

206
00:08:39,875 --> 00:08:42,375
This man must confess,

207
00:08:42,416 --> 00:08:44,541
That at the instigation of that vile man,

208
00:08:44,583 --> 00:08:46,000
He came to my house to steal!

209
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:47,666
He must say that that man,

210
00:08:47,666 --> 00:08:49,125
Instigated him!

211
00:08:49,208 --> 00:08:50,875
If he won’t talk!

212
00:08:50,875 --> 00:08:52,125
If he doesn’t confess,

213
00:08:52,166 --> 00:08:54,166
Tomorrow I’ll hang him on the gallows in the garden!

214
00:08:54,541 --> 00:08:55,708
Conspiracy!

215
00:08:56,375 --> 00:08:57,875
Conspiracy!

216
00:08:58,500 --> 00:08:59,750
Conspiracy!

217
00:08:59,916 --> 00:09:02,500
All these people conspired against me!

218
00:09:06,083 --> 00:09:09,166
♪ Sound of military march ♪

219
00:09:21,666 --> 00:09:22,750
What are you doing, Mash Ghasem?

220
00:09:22,791 --> 00:09:24,541
Kid, hurry back to your own house!

221
00:09:24,583 --> 00:09:25,583
What happened!

222
00:09:26,708 --> 00:09:28,416
Today is doomsday!

223
00:09:28,583 --> 00:09:31,125
Tell your dad and mom to stay away from here.

224
00:09:31,291 --> 00:09:32,583
And you get going too, kid!

225
00:09:33,750 --> 00:09:34,541
Why!

226
00:09:34,583 --> 00:09:36,583
What happened again, Mash Ghasem?

227
00:09:36,625 --> 00:09:38,375
Honestly, son, why should I lie?

228
00:09:38,625 --> 00:09:40,375
The grave is this close!

229
00:09:40,541 --> 00:09:42,083
We’re very worried today.

230
00:09:42,500 --> 00:09:43,750
Sir ordered,

231
00:09:43,750 --> 00:09:46,208
If any of you sets foot past this tree,

232
00:09:46,250 --> 00:09:48,000
We shoot him right through the heart!

233
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:48,833
Why?

234
00:09:48,875 --> 00:09:50,166
Didn’t you say what happened?

235
00:09:50,541 --> 00:09:51,833
Last night when you went,

236
00:09:52,083 --> 00:09:53,000
We caught the thief.

237
00:09:53,541 --> 00:09:54,458
Well, we didn’t catch him…

238
00:09:54,500 --> 00:09:56,250
This Shir-Ali… the same butcher,

239
00:09:56,458 --> 00:09:57,541
Caught him on the roof,

240
00:09:57,583 --> 00:09:58,291
And brought him home!

241
00:09:58,708 --> 00:09:59,541
What did you do with him?

242
00:09:59,958 --> 00:10:00,958
Honestly, why should I lie!

243
00:10:01,666 --> 00:10:03,333
Shir-Ali wanted to take a cleaver right there

244
00:10:03,333 --> 00:10:04,291
And split him in two!

245
00:10:04,875 --> 00:10:06,208
But Sir said no.

246
00:10:06,208 --> 00:10:07,708
Well, we put in a word for him too.

247
00:10:08,958 --> 00:10:11,541
Now he’s tied up with rope, locked in the basement.

248
00:10:11,541 --> 00:10:12,250
And we’re guarding him.

249
00:10:12,791 --> 00:10:13,750
In the basement!

250
00:10:14,041 --> 00:10:15,916
Why didn’t you turn him in?

251
00:10:15,916 --> 00:10:17,958
You have no idea, kid!

252
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:19,541
Sir wants to hang him today,

253
00:10:19,541 --> 00:10:20,916
On the gallows in the garden!

254
00:10:23,333 --> 00:10:24,291
Hang him on the gallows?

255
00:10:24,583 --> 00:10:26,083
Stop talking to us, go!

256
00:10:26,083 --> 00:10:27,791
If Sir finds out you talked with us,

257
00:10:27,791 --> 00:10:29,416
He might hang us too.

258
00:10:29,833 --> 00:10:30,625
But Mash Ghasem,

259
00:10:30,666 --> 00:10:32,250
What’s catching a thief got to do with us?

260
00:10:32,250 --> 00:10:34,208
Why is Dear Uncle angry with us?

261
00:10:34,291 --> 00:10:36,000
If you knew who the thief is,

262
00:10:36,041 --> 00:10:38,041
Then you’d understand what it has to do with you!

263
00:10:39,041 --> 00:10:40,125
The situation is bad!

264
00:10:40,166 --> 00:10:41,666
Oh dear, oh dear, God help us!

265
00:10:46,166 --> 00:10:48,125
God, please let this end well.

266
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:55,375
Who is the thief, Mash Ghasem?

267
00:10:55,416 --> 00:10:56,625
What did he steal?

268
00:10:56,750 --> 00:10:57,875
Honestly, why should I lie…

269
00:10:57,916 --> 00:10:59,708
The grave is this close! - Ghasem

270
00:11:00,958 --> 00:11:02,875
Oh, good Lord! Sir is coming… go!

271
00:11:02,875 --> 00:11:04,375
Come on, run… if you value your life!

272
00:11:04,416 --> 00:11:04,958
Escape!

273
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:05,625
Hide!

274
00:11:19,708 --> 00:11:20,291
Ghasem!

275
00:11:20,333 --> 00:11:21,541
Yes, Sir!

276
00:11:21,583 --> 00:11:23,375
Weren’t you told, once your work was done,

277
00:11:23,416 --> 00:11:24,500
Guard the thief!

278
00:11:24,500 --> 00:11:25,875
Rest assured, Sir!

279
00:11:25,916 --> 00:11:27,166
The thief is in the basement,

280
00:11:27,166 --> 00:11:28,416
We’re watching him from right here.

281
00:11:29,500 --> 00:11:31,083
Watching him, are you!

282
00:11:31,208 --> 00:11:33,625
You can’t leave him without food and water!

283
00:11:33,916 --> 00:11:35,625
And keeping him costs money!

284
00:11:36,208 --> 00:11:37,500
Now what do you want to do, Sir?

285
00:11:37,750 --> 00:11:38,875
Hang him on the gallows?

286
00:11:39,125 --> 00:11:39,916
- Huh?

287
00:11:57,458 --> 00:11:59,958
We must get him to confess!

288
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:00,916
From whom, Sir?

289
00:12:01,083 --> 00:12:02,333
From that one!

290
00:12:08,875 --> 00:12:10,333
Your sister’s husband?!

291
00:12:10,750 --> 00:12:13,041
That one is not my sister’s husband!

292
00:12:13,041 --> 00:12:16,166
You remember that this same Hamdollah was his servant for several years?

293
00:12:16,166 --> 00:12:18,000
Yes, Sir, back then he wasn’t a thief,

294
00:12:18,041 --> 00:12:19,083
He was a God-fearing man!

295
00:12:19,250 --> 00:12:20,875
Now that same God-fearing person,

296
00:12:20,916 --> 00:12:22,291
Came to my house to steal!

297
00:12:25,291 --> 00:12:27,166
It’s clear they instigated him!

298
00:12:27,333 --> 00:12:30,250
There is no doubt a dirty conspiracy is at work!

299
00:12:30,416 --> 00:12:31,416
You know, Ghasem!

300
00:12:31,458 --> 00:12:33,375
Now I am worried about this,

301
00:12:33,416 --> 00:12:35,541
That this foul-mouthed man

302
00:12:35,583 --> 00:12:37,875
Will go around everywhere,

303
00:12:37,875 --> 00:12:40,458
Making us a laughing-stock!

304
00:12:40,458 --> 00:12:41,708
Who would dare mock you?

305
00:12:41,708 --> 00:12:43,041
That one!

306
00:12:43,041 --> 00:12:44,291
So how about, Sir,

307
00:12:44,333 --> 00:12:46,166
You just forget all this talk,

308
00:12:46,166 --> 00:12:48,708
And kiss and make up so it all ends well.

309
00:12:48,708 --> 00:12:52,125
Me, make peace with that filthy man!?

310
00:12:52,166 --> 00:12:52,916
Huh!?

311
00:12:52,958 --> 00:12:54,541
We… we said nothing, Sir!

312
00:12:54,541 --> 00:12:55,916
Why don’t you understand!

313
00:12:55,958 --> 00:12:57,916
Have you forgotten last night?

314
00:12:58,416 --> 00:13:01,541
Well… last night I wasn’t feeling well and…

315
00:13:01,583 --> 00:13:03,333
I felt a little sick.

316
00:13:04,541 --> 00:13:05,875
You remember,

317
00:13:05,916 --> 00:13:07,625
As he was going out the door,

318
00:13:07,625 --> 00:13:09,291
He turned back and said what?

319
00:13:09,583 --> 00:13:10,916
Honestly, Sir, why should I lie?

320
00:13:10,916 --> 00:13:13,291
The grave is this close!

321
00:13:13,333 --> 00:13:14,791
We don’t remember a thing.

322
00:13:14,833 --> 00:13:16,833
How can you not remember?

323
00:13:21,458 --> 00:13:22,625
He said one word,

324
00:13:23,000 --> 00:13:24,500
Which meant, in other words,

325
00:13:24,500 --> 00:13:27,708
That I feared a thief!

326
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:29,166
God forbid!

327
00:13:29,250 --> 00:13:30,916
You and fear?

328
00:13:31,166 --> 00:13:32,666
That’s just it!

329
00:13:33,166 --> 00:13:36,458
Even if no one knows, you know very well

330
00:13:36,583 --> 00:13:37,875
You always,

331
00:13:37,875 --> 00:13:38,750
In wars,

332
00:13:38,791 --> 00:13:39,708
On the battlefields,

333
00:13:39,708 --> 00:13:42,000
You were with me!

334
00:13:42,041 --> 00:13:45,208
You know that in my dictionary,

335
00:13:45,375 --> 00:13:48,208
Fear does not exist!

336
00:13:50,083 --> 00:13:51,791
Honest to God…

337
00:13:51,791 --> 00:13:54,625
Such accusations don’t stick to you!

338
00:13:56,041 --> 00:13:57,416
I remember…

339
00:13:58,083 --> 00:14:00,666
Sultan Ali Khan, may God rest his soul…

340
00:14:01,041 --> 00:14:03,041
Before the Kazerun war he was saying…

341
00:14:03,500 --> 00:14:06,000
All that recklessness and fearlessness

342
00:14:06,041 --> 00:14:07,458
Will get Sir into trouble one day!

343
00:14:08,666 --> 00:14:11,458
You remember that night they poured into our tent?

344
00:14:11,750 --> 00:14:13,000
As if it was yesterday…

345
00:14:13,958 --> 00:14:17,500
You brought down three of the bandits with one bullet!

346
00:14:17,541 --> 00:14:19,416
Bravo!

347
00:14:19,458 --> 00:14:20,416
(He chuckles under his breath)

348
00:14:22,166 --> 00:14:25,166
Those were merciless thieves, back then!

349
00:14:26,166 --> 00:14:27,875
Today’s thieves…

350
00:14:27,916 --> 00:14:30,541
Are babes in arms compared to them.

351
00:14:30,833 --> 00:14:32,041
Even we,

352
00:14:32,041 --> 00:14:34,416
Who were so reckless and fearless,

353
00:14:34,416 --> 00:14:36,125
God knows it,

354
00:14:36,166 --> 00:14:37,708
And you may as well know it too:

355
00:14:38,041 --> 00:14:39,375
That night we were very afraid.

356
00:14:39,916 --> 00:14:42,541
You remember the leader of the thieves?

357
00:14:42,583 --> 00:14:44,208
How he fell at your feet,

358
00:14:44,250 --> 00:14:45,916
Begging and pleading!?

359
00:14:47,500 --> 00:14:49,208
As if it was yesterday!

360
00:14:50,291 --> 00:14:51,250
His name…

361
00:14:51,458 --> 00:14:52,750
Wasn’t it Sed Morad?

362
00:14:53,250 --> 00:14:55,166
We’ve seen plenty of Sed Morads!

363
00:14:57,250 --> 00:14:59,375
May his holy ancestors curse him!

364
00:14:59,875 --> 00:15:02,750
What a merciless and dishonorable person he was!

365
00:15:03,375 --> 00:15:04,416
But Ghasem…

366
00:15:04,458 --> 00:15:05,708
You and I know that.

367
00:15:07,416 --> 00:15:08,458
If today,

368
00:15:09,458 --> 00:15:11,250
That vile man,

369
00:15:11,750 --> 00:15:13,791
With that foul-mouthed doctor,

370
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:17,708
Go around saying that so-and-so

371
00:15:17,750 --> 00:15:20,291
Took ill from fear of a thief…

372
00:15:20,333 --> 00:15:26,083
Then what becomes of my lifelong reputation!

373
00:15:26,083 --> 00:15:27,333
Oh!

374
00:15:27,333 --> 00:15:28,875
Who will believe, Sir?

375
00:15:28,875 --> 00:15:30,041
In the land of Iran,

376
00:15:30,041 --> 00:15:32,208
Who doesn’t know how brave you are?

377
00:15:32,208 --> 00:15:35,166
People believe whatever they hear!

378
00:15:35,208 --> 00:15:37,875
I am sure that that dishonorable man,

379
00:15:37,916 --> 00:15:40,708
To damage my reputation and honor,

380
00:15:40,708 --> 00:15:43,583
Plotted that conspiracy last night!

381
00:15:43,625 --> 00:15:44,250
Today also,

382
00:15:44,250 --> 00:15:45,125
They’ll all go

383
00:15:45,166 --> 00:15:47,041
And trumpet it from the rooftops,

384
00:15:47,041 --> 00:15:48,458
(Makes the sound of playing the instrument)

385
00:15:48,500 --> 00:15:50,708
And we’ll tell everyone they’re lying!

386
00:15:51,458 --> 00:15:53,958
We’ll just say Sir was feeling sick.

387
00:15:54,791 --> 00:15:55,500
We’ll say…

388
00:15:55,750 --> 00:15:57,083
A snake bit Sir!

389
00:15:57,416 --> 00:15:59,958
Why talk nonsense, Ghasem?!

390
00:16:00,208 --> 00:16:01,916
If a snake bites someone,

391
00:16:01,958 --> 00:16:03,750
Does he recover this quickly?!

392
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:05,166
Why wouldn’t he?!

393
00:16:05,750 --> 00:16:07,166
We had a fellow villager…

394
00:16:07,166 --> 00:16:09,208
Never mind your fellow villager…

395
00:16:09,375 --> 00:16:11,375
Enough talk, go bring the thief!

396
00:16:11,791 --> 00:16:13,875
He must confess that,

397
00:16:13,916 --> 00:16:16,041
That dishonorable man conspired against me!

398
00:16:16,708 --> 00:16:18,708
Why delay? Go bring the thief!

399
00:16:18,916 --> 00:16:20,666
Sir, if you ask us…

400
00:16:20,708 --> 00:16:22,166
I didn’t ask you anything!

401
00:16:22,208 --> 00:16:24,166
I… I… I… I mean, if you ask us…

402
00:16:24,208 --> 00:16:27,083
We’d say it’s better to let the thief go.

403
00:16:27,166 --> 00:16:28,000
Let him go?!

404
00:16:28,416 --> 00:16:29,916
Let the thief go!

405
00:16:29,958 --> 00:16:32,458
If word gets out that we caught a thief,

406
00:16:32,500 --> 00:16:33,541
Then that one,

407
00:16:33,541 --> 00:16:35,041
Your sister’s husband,

408
00:16:35,083 --> 00:16:37,250
Will tell the story of last night everywhere!

409
00:16:37,500 --> 00:16:40,083
Then all of Iran will be buzzing

410
00:16:40,125 --> 00:16:42,541
That Sir feared a thief! (He cries)

411
00:16:42,583 --> 00:16:44,625
(Sound of birds singing)

412
00:16:52,291 --> 00:16:53,583
It’s none of our business, Sir…

413
00:16:53,583 --> 00:16:55,833
But you’d better let this Hamdollah go.

414
00:16:55,833 --> 00:16:57,208
The trouble will blow over too.

415
00:16:57,916 --> 00:17:00,500
Right now no one except Shir-Ali the butcher,

416
00:17:00,500 --> 00:17:02,333
Knows that we caught a thief.

417
00:17:02,791 --> 00:17:06,000
I mean, no outsider knows we caught a thief.

418
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:08,458
And Shir-Ali’s on our side, he won’t say a word.

419
00:17:12,875 --> 00:17:17,916
Do a good deed and… throw it in the Tigris

420
00:17:19,375 --> 00:17:21,916
So God repays you in your hour of need.

421
00:17:24,333 --> 00:17:26,333
Always, in our family,

422
00:17:26,541 --> 00:17:29,208
Forgiveness and generosity have been our custom.

423
00:17:30,291 --> 00:17:32,291
For the health of the children,

424
00:17:32,333 --> 00:17:34,333
We’ll forgive this wretch his sin.

425
00:17:35,083 --> 00:17:35,875
Ghasem…

426
00:17:37,833 --> 00:17:39,791
Go untie his hands and feet and,

427
00:17:40,208 --> 00:17:42,208
Tell him to hit the road and go quickly.

428
00:17:42,708 --> 00:17:44,625
Especially tell him,

429
00:17:44,791 --> 00:17:47,250
That you’re doing this on your own.

430
00:17:47,375 --> 00:17:49,291
Tell him that if Sir finds out,

431
00:17:49,333 --> 00:17:50,875
He’ll skin me alive!

432
00:18:02,833 --> 00:18:06,125
So God repays you in your hour of need…

433
00:18:20,333 --> 00:18:21,375
Are you going to the pharmacy?

434
00:18:21,375 --> 00:18:22,166
No!

435
00:18:22,416 --> 00:18:23,583
If they come from the pharmacy,

436
00:18:23,583 --> 00:18:24,958
Tell them to stay, I’ll be back soon.

437
00:18:28,958 --> 00:18:31,208
Maybe we’ll have a few guests tonight.

438
00:18:31,500 --> 00:18:32,291
Guests?!

439
00:18:32,500 --> 00:18:33,958
Then why didn’t you say sooner?

440
00:18:38,416 --> 00:18:39,791
God give you long life, Mash Ghasem.

441
00:18:39,875 --> 00:18:41,125
As long as I live, I’m your servant. - Go… go, Hamdollah!

442
00:18:41,125 --> 00:18:42,541
Don’t let yourself be seen around here again!

443
00:18:42,541 --> 00:18:44,791
Go on, son, off you go. Good luck!

444
00:18:53,541 --> 00:18:55,666
May God keep you with us always.

445
00:18:56,208 --> 00:18:57,958
You don’t know how much he prayed.

446
00:18:58,666 --> 00:19:00,500
You remember that same Sed Morad…

447
00:19:00,791 --> 00:19:03,125
Once he begged and pleaded, you forgave him.

448
00:19:03,291 --> 00:19:04,041
Plus!

449
00:19:04,083 --> 00:19:06,750
You even gave him money for the road.

450
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:07,833
Ghasem…

451
00:19:08,291 --> 00:19:10,791
Who appreciates these things?

452
00:19:11,166 --> 00:19:12,958
Maybe it would have been better,

453
00:19:12,958 --> 00:19:15,708
If I too, like all powerful people,

454
00:19:15,750 --> 00:19:18,791
Had been merciless and cruel to others.

455
00:19:19,208 --> 00:19:20,833
This very merciful heart of mine,

456
00:19:20,875 --> 00:19:23,583
Has held me back in life.

457
00:19:23,625 --> 00:19:25,458
Don’t say that, Sir!

458
00:19:25,458 --> 00:19:27,875
What we know, the whole world knows.

459
00:19:29,750 --> 00:19:32,583
If foreigners didn’t have a hand in it,

460
00:19:33,875 --> 00:19:35,666
Just the day before yesterday… (He speaks quietly and secretly)

461
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:38,416
At the bazaar, they talked about you.

462
00:19:38,833 --> 00:19:39,958
I said, Sir,

463
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:41,958
If the English didn’t have it in for you,

464
00:19:42,000 --> 00:19:44,333
Just think what you’d have done by now!

465
00:19:44,791 --> 00:19:47,041
If not for the English, (He speaks quietly)

466
00:19:47,041 --> 00:19:49,125
If their agents weren’t everywhere!

467
00:19:49,125 --> 00:19:51,416
Just think what I’d have done by now!

468
00:19:52,583 --> 00:19:55,875
Really, Sir, why are the English so bad with you?

469
00:19:55,916 --> 00:19:57,833
This treacherous wolf…

470
00:19:57,875 --> 00:19:59,125
England!

471
00:19:59,166 --> 00:20:02,000
Anyone who loves his homeland,

472
00:20:02,041 --> 00:20:03,000
Is its enemy!

473
00:20:04,958 --> 00:20:07,958
What sin had Napoleon committed,

474
00:20:08,208 --> 00:20:11,291
That they brought him to ruin like that!

475
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:15,500
Separated him from wife and child like that.

476
00:20:15,583 --> 00:20:18,750
Exiled him to Saint Helena island!

477
00:20:19,291 --> 00:20:22,166
Made him die of grief!

478
00:20:23,625 --> 00:20:24,666
Simply,

479
00:20:25,125 --> 00:20:26,708
He loved his homeland.

480
00:20:28,958 --> 00:20:29,833
This,

481
00:20:30,250 --> 00:20:32,125
In the eyes of the English,

482
00:20:32,291 --> 00:20:34,375
Was his greatest sin!

483
00:20:36,125 --> 00:20:37,708
I pray to God, by Imam Ali,

484
00:20:37,750 --> 00:20:39,333
May they never know a moment’s peace!

485
00:20:39,375 --> 00:20:41,750
The English enmity with me,

486
00:20:42,125 --> 00:20:44,625
Started from the time they saw,

487
00:20:44,875 --> 00:20:47,125
I love my homeland!

488
00:20:47,625 --> 00:20:49,500
I want freedom.

489
00:20:49,750 --> 00:20:52,000
I want a constitution.

490
00:20:52,041 --> 00:20:54,625
Now everyone claims they were for the constitution!

491
00:20:54,666 --> 00:20:56,958
They suffered for freedom!

492
00:20:57,250 --> 00:20:59,375
They did this, they did that.

493
00:20:59,375 --> 00:21:00,583
But these same ones,

494
00:21:00,583 --> 00:21:03,000
When Mamdali Shah bombarded the parliament,

495
00:21:03,041 --> 00:21:06,041
They scurried into their holes like mice!

496
00:21:06,083 --> 00:21:08,708
But we didn’t talk about ourselves. (He laughs)

497
00:21:08,875 --> 00:21:11,000
We got lost in memories.

498
00:21:11,041 --> 00:21:13,166
Worthless son of a bitch!

499
00:21:13,416 --> 00:21:14,500
Eh…

500
00:21:14,500 --> 00:21:16,708
Ghasem, rifle!

501
00:21:16,750 --> 00:21:18,000
Oh, good Lord!

502
00:21:18,291 --> 00:21:20,250
The Cossacks of Colonel Liakhov too, - I said give me the rifle!

503
00:21:20,250 --> 00:21:22,916
Are now fighters for the constitution!

504
00:21:23,000 --> 00:21:25,041
I said give me the rifle!

505
00:21:25,083 --> 00:21:25,916
Have pity, Sir.

506
00:21:25,958 --> 00:21:27,500
Give me the rifle!

507
00:21:27,541 --> 00:21:28,583
Forgive him.

508
00:21:28,791 --> 00:21:31,208
Why run, traitor!

509
00:21:31,250 --> 00:21:31,708
Sir!

510
00:21:31,750 --> 00:21:32,666
Give me the rifle,

511
00:21:32,666 --> 00:21:34,458
So I can silence him!

512
00:21:34,500 --> 00:21:35,291
Sir, have pity!

513
00:21:35,375 --> 00:21:36,958
I said stop!

514
00:21:37,416 --> 00:21:38,541
Ghasem!

515
00:21:38,541 --> 00:21:39,333
Sir, forgive him.

516
00:21:39,333 --> 00:21:40,875
Damn you!

517
00:21:41,125 --> 00:21:43,583
If my hand reaches you,

518
00:21:44,000 --> 00:21:46,000
I will rain bullets on you.

519
00:21:46,000 --> 00:21:46,375
Sir!

520
00:21:46,416 --> 00:21:47,125
Have pity!

521
00:21:47,166 --> 00:21:48,666
I will hang you.

522
00:21:48,666 --> 00:21:49,541
Forgive him.

523
00:21:49,541 --> 00:21:51,125
I said give me the rifle! - Sir!

524
00:21:51,500 --> 00:21:52,458
Traitor!

525
00:21:52,750 --> 00:21:54,250
Ungrateful!

526
00:21:54,250 --> 00:21:55,375
Give me!

527
00:21:55,375 --> 00:21:57,291
Give me the rifle! - Sir!

528
00:21:57,291 --> 00:21:58,500
Sir… have pity! - I can’t

529
00:21:58,583 --> 00:22:00,666
Give me the rifle!

530
00:22:00,791 --> 00:22:02,250
Give me!

531
00:22:02,500 --> 00:22:02,958
Give!

532
00:22:03,166 --> 00:22:04,875
Before I throttle you! (He starts panting)

533
00:22:09,916 --> 00:22:10,916
Give me!

534
00:22:12,041 --> 00:22:13,041
Give me!

535
00:22:13,208 --> 00:22:14,541
I’m out of breath…

536
00:22:18,541 --> 00:22:20,333
Traitor, give me that rifle!

537
00:22:20,541 --> 00:22:22,125
I’ll make you pay!

538
00:22:24,000 --> 00:22:25,000
Oh, good Lord!

539
00:22:26,333 --> 00:22:28,250
Ow, ow, we’re dead, Sir!

540
00:22:28,666 --> 00:22:30,208
(He groans)

541
00:22:30,291 --> 00:22:32,125
Mash Ghasem, Mash Ghasem… what happened?

542
00:22:32,166 --> 00:22:32,708
Run!

543
00:22:32,750 --> 00:22:34,875
Run, bring Doctor Naser Al-hokama! - Sir, you killed your Ghasem!

544
00:22:35,208 --> 00:22:36,250
Why stand there? - Are you alive, Mash Ghasem?

545
00:22:36,250 --> 00:22:38,916
Run, my dear, run, bring the doctor…

546
00:22:38,958 --> 00:22:40,625
(Sound of groaning)

547
00:22:40,666 --> 00:22:43,750
Sir, you killed your Ghasem, Sir!

548
00:22:44,166 --> 00:22:46,208
Sir, help us! (He groans)

549
00:22:46,208 --> 00:22:47,791
Ghasem… - Sir…

550
00:22:47,833 --> 00:22:49,291
Ghasem…

551
00:22:49,291 --> 00:22:50,208
Sir… (He groans)

552
00:22:50,250 --> 00:22:52,375
What happened to Ghasem! (He cries)

553
00:22:52,416 --> 00:22:53,833
(He groans)

554
00:22:53,875 --> 00:22:54,625
Ghasem!

555
00:22:54,666 --> 00:22:55,708
Sir, don’t touch us,

556
00:22:55,708 --> 00:22:58,083
Let us die right here…

557
00:22:58,125 --> 00:22:59,708
From what you say,

558
00:22:59,750 --> 00:23:02,166
Your patient must have a chill in the stomach.

559
00:23:02,166 --> 00:23:04,125
Let me see… how is his digestion?

560
00:23:04,166 --> 00:23:05,833
Does he answer nature’s call?

561
00:23:05,833 --> 00:23:07,125
Eh, not bad, Mr. Doctor.

562
00:23:07,125 --> 00:23:09,375
But his stomach ache doesn’t get better.

563
00:23:09,416 --> 00:23:11,125
It will get better, dear… it will get better.

564
00:23:11,166 --> 00:23:12,500
Don’t worry.

565
00:23:12,541 --> 00:23:15,541
You might give him some hot rock-candy tea.

566
00:23:15,541 --> 00:23:17,875
We did, Mr. Doctor, but it didn’t help.

567
00:23:18,000 --> 00:23:19,958
Very well… let’s go see what it is…

568
00:23:21,291 --> 00:23:22,166
Sir!

569
00:23:22,208 --> 00:23:23,208
Mr. Doctor! - What is it?

570
00:23:23,208 --> 00:23:24,541
Mr. Doctor… - What is it, my dear?

571
00:23:24,583 --> 00:23:26,000
Mr. Doctor, run!

572
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:27,708
Stay well. - Run!

573
00:23:27,708 --> 00:23:28,583
Mash Ghasem!

574
00:23:28,583 --> 00:23:29,708
Stay well… - What happened?

575
00:23:29,708 --> 00:23:30,583
- He got shot! - Anyone dead?

576
00:23:30,625 --> 00:23:31,958
He got shot… - Shot?

577
00:23:31,958 --> 00:23:33,333
His condition is bad!

578
00:23:33,375 --> 00:23:36,250
(Sound of crowd noise)

579
00:23:36,291 --> 00:23:38,666
Let me see, my dear! Let me see… - What happened, Mr. Doctor!

580
00:23:38,708 --> 00:23:39,791
- Anyone dead?

581
00:23:39,791 --> 00:23:40,583
- I don’t know either!

582
00:23:40,625 --> 00:23:42,583
How do I know if he’s dead or not!

583
00:23:43,666 --> 00:23:45,500
Ghasem… enough! (Sound of groaning)

584
00:23:45,541 --> 00:23:45,958
What is it?

585
00:23:45,958 --> 00:23:47,375
What happened? - Nothing’s wrong with him.

586
00:23:47,416 --> 00:23:48,875
My stomach….. ouch…

587
00:23:48,875 --> 00:23:50,750
It hurts…

588
00:23:50,791 --> 00:23:52,250
It burns…

589
00:23:52,291 --> 00:23:53,208
All right… drink water

590
00:23:54,666 --> 00:23:57,750
I’ll go to my grave without ever seeing Mecca.

591
00:23:57,750 --> 00:23:59,750
- Why are you talking nonsense, Mash Ghasem?

592
00:23:59,750 --> 00:24:01,000
- Nothing’s wrong with you! - Sir…

593
00:24:01,000 --> 00:24:02,208
Dear Sir…

594
00:24:02,250 --> 00:24:05,208
Your Ghasem is dying!

595
00:24:05,250 --> 00:24:07,083
- Mash Ghasem, stop it already! (Sound of groaning)

596
00:24:07,083 --> 00:24:08,666
Promise me

597
00:24:08,708 --> 00:24:10,250
In the shrine of Hazrat Masumeh,

598
00:24:10,250 --> 00:24:11,125
They’ll bury us.

599
00:24:11,125 --> 00:24:13,083
It must have just grazed him…

600
00:24:13,125 --> 00:24:14,291
Oh God…

601
00:24:14,333 --> 00:24:16,208
(Sound of groaning)

602
00:24:16,250 --> 00:24:17,791
- Don’t touch, child!

603
00:24:17,833 --> 00:24:19,125
God…

604
00:24:19,166 --> 00:24:19,958
- Don’t move!

605
00:24:20,000 --> 00:24:22,750
Take that rifle from his hand!

606
00:24:22,750 --> 00:24:24,916
Get up, take it from him… get up already! (Sound of groaning)

607
00:24:24,916 --> 00:24:26,250
Go take it from him… run!

608
00:24:26,541 --> 00:24:27,416
Go!

609
00:24:27,666 --> 00:24:28,958
- Ah… God…!

610
00:24:29,000 --> 00:24:30,166
Give… - Surrender, surrender!

611
00:24:30,208 --> 00:24:32,000
Dad… m… mom!

612
00:24:32,000 --> 00:24:33,875
Mommy dear!

613
00:24:33,875 --> 00:24:35,666
Mom… mom!

614
00:24:36,250 --> 00:24:37,625
Who told you to take that rifle?

615
00:24:38,416 --> 00:24:39,375
- Stay well!

616
00:24:39,375 --> 00:24:41,083
- Feels like a snake bit our belly!

617
00:24:41,083 --> 00:24:42,041
- Stay well!

618
00:24:42,041 --> 00:24:43,500
Hello ladies! - Hello Mr. Doctor

619
00:24:43,500 --> 00:24:44,500
Welcome!

620
00:24:44,541 --> 00:24:46,416
(Sound of groaning)

621
00:24:46,458 --> 00:24:49,208
Mash Ghasem… enough already! - Oh, good Lord

622
00:24:49,208 --> 00:24:51,541
Oh no…

623
00:24:51,583 --> 00:24:53,375
Honestly nothing’s wrong with you!

624
00:24:53,416 --> 00:24:55,125
Mash Ghasem, don’t be afraid!

625
00:24:55,166 --> 00:24:57,291
Oh, good Lord… don’t touch me!

626
00:24:57,291 --> 00:24:59,166
Don’t touch me… oh…

627
00:24:59,208 --> 00:25:00,041
Mash Ghasem!

628
00:25:00,041 --> 00:25:01,166
It’s Mr. Doctor!

629
00:25:01,208 --> 00:25:02,291
Hello Mr. Doctor!

630
00:25:02,333 --> 00:25:03,041
- Stay well!

631
00:25:03,041 --> 00:25:04,250
First you, then God!

632
00:25:04,291 --> 00:25:06,000
First God, Mash Ghasem!

633
00:25:06,000 --> 00:25:07,166
Same difference!

634
00:25:07,166 --> 00:25:08,791
Stay well! - Ay…

635
00:25:08,833 --> 00:25:10,125
Stay well! (Sound of groaning)

636
00:25:10,166 --> 00:25:11,708
God forgive us!

637
00:25:11,750 --> 00:25:15,166
(Sound of groaning)

638
00:25:15,208 --> 00:25:17,625
Well… tell me… how did it happen?

639
00:25:17,625 --> 00:25:18,666
What happened? - He got shot!

640
00:25:18,666 --> 00:25:22,250
(Sound of groaning)

641
00:25:22,250 --> 00:25:23,791
Where did the bullet hit you?

642
00:25:24,791 --> 00:25:26,500
Who shot you?

643
00:25:26,791 --> 00:25:28,291
Where did it hit?

644
00:25:28,333 --> 00:25:31,375
(He groans louder) - Who shot you?

645
00:25:31,375 --> 00:25:33,041
Tell me, who did it?

646
00:25:33,041 --> 00:25:33,625
That one!

647
00:25:33,666 --> 00:25:36,250
That murderer, that merciless murderer!

648
00:25:36,250 --> 00:25:38,000
And what do you want, spy!

649
00:25:38,333 --> 00:25:39,416
With my own hands,

650
00:25:39,458 --> 00:25:41,166
I’ll put the noose around your neck!

651
00:25:41,208 --> 00:25:43,708
What business do you have with people’s affairs anyway?

652
00:25:43,750 --> 00:25:46,041
Are you the local snoop, spy!

653
00:25:46,083 --> 00:25:47,416
- God help me! - I’m the spy?

654
00:25:47,458 --> 00:25:49,208
If I’m a spy, you’re a murderer! - You cheating bastard!

655
00:25:49,208 --> 00:25:51,125
- You cheating bastard!

656
00:25:51,125 --> 00:25:54,208
(Sound of commotion and fighting)

657
00:25:54,916 --> 00:25:55,625
Saeid!

658
00:25:56,291 --> 00:25:57,833
He wants to kill Agha Joon! - I swear I’ll put a noose around your neck!

659
00:25:57,833 --> 00:25:58,416
Who?

660
00:25:58,416 --> 00:25:58,458
He wants to kill Agha Joon! - I swear I’ll put a noose around your neck!

661
00:25:58,458 --> 00:25:59,125
Dear Uncle!

662
00:25:59,166 --> 00:26:01,333
(Sound of commotion and fighting)

663
00:26:01,333 --> 00:26:02,458
For God’s sake, don’t get angry!

664
00:26:02,500 --> 00:26:05,375
- With my own hands I’ll strangle him! - Man, stop it, shame on you!

665
00:26:05,375 --> 00:26:09,833
- Stay well, stay well! - I’ll make you miserable!

666
00:26:09,833 --> 00:26:11,958
- Man… shame on you!

667
00:26:11,958 --> 00:26:13,625
- I’ll bring the house down on your head!

668
00:26:13,666 --> 00:26:16,291
It’s shameful! Come on, go! (Sound of commotion and fighting)

669
00:26:16,291 --> 00:26:17,708
- Crazy idiot!

670
00:26:17,708 --> 00:26:20,500
- Brother Khan is the elder, go inside! - I’ll make you pay!

671
00:26:21,083 --> 00:26:22,500
Honestly, Mr. Doctor, why should I lie!

672
00:26:22,541 --> 00:26:24,083
The grave is this close!

673
00:26:24,125 --> 00:26:25,666
Where did the bullet hit you?!

674
00:26:26,250 --> 00:26:28,416
Say ah… - Seems it’s somewhere in our side…

675
00:26:30,291 --> 00:26:31,416
Ouch…

676
00:26:31,458 --> 00:26:33,666
We’ve fought in so many wars and battles,

677
00:26:33,708 --> 00:26:36,875
Only to meet our end in Sir’s garden!

678
00:26:37,500 --> 00:26:38,708
Mr. Doctor…

679
00:26:38,750 --> 00:26:39,750
For God’s sake,

680
00:26:39,750 --> 00:26:41,583
Tell us the truth in our final moment.

681
00:26:41,625 --> 00:26:43,458
If we’re done for,

682
00:26:43,500 --> 00:26:46,250
If there’s no hope of us surviving,

683
00:26:46,250 --> 00:26:48,583
Tell us, so we can pray.

684
00:26:48,625 --> 00:26:50,708
Nothing has happened to you, my dear! (He roars)

685
00:26:50,708 --> 00:26:52,833
(He roars)

686
00:26:52,833 --> 00:26:54,916
(Sound of groaning)

687
00:27:02,541 --> 00:27:03,916
What is it?

688
00:27:04,291 --> 00:27:06,250
Why are you crying so much?

689
00:27:10,666 --> 00:27:12,958
So where did the bullet hit you?

690
00:27:14,000 --> 00:27:15,333
Honestly, Sir, why lie?

691
00:27:15,333 --> 00:27:16,750
Truth is, how would we know?

692
00:27:16,750 --> 00:27:18,500
You’re the doctor, can’t you tell?

693
00:27:18,541 --> 00:27:21,666
Stay well! Stay well!

694
00:27:21,666 --> 00:27:24,208
He’s healthier than I am!

695
00:27:24,541 --> 00:27:26,708
Now you lie to me too, you cheating swindler?

696
00:27:26,750 --> 00:27:28,125
Get up, go get lost!

697
00:27:28,166 --> 00:27:29,166
When did we lie to you, Sir!

698
00:27:29,166 --> 00:27:32,708
When did we ever lie to you, sir?!

699
00:27:34,458 --> 00:27:36,583
You mean we didn’t get shot!

700
00:27:36,625 --> 00:27:38,583
Then what was that pain and burning?

701
00:27:38,583 --> 00:27:39,666
Then where did the bullet hit us?

702
00:27:39,708 --> 00:27:41,250
I wish it had hit your brain!

703
00:27:41,458 --> 00:27:43,291
Why are you picking on him!?

704
00:27:43,458 --> 00:27:46,041
If he really had been shot,

705
00:27:46,083 --> 00:27:47,750
Would that make you happy?

706
00:27:47,750 --> 00:27:50,166
(Sound of groaning)

707
00:27:50,208 --> 00:27:53,125
Stay well, stay well…

708
00:27:55,166 --> 00:27:56,666
Thank God a hundred thousand times,

709
00:27:56,666 --> 00:27:58,833
That we didn’t get shot!

710
00:28:01,500 --> 00:28:03,500
M… M… Mr. Doctor!

711
00:28:03,500 --> 00:28:04,791
Mr. Doctor!

712
00:28:04,791 --> 00:28:06,875
Yes? Go ahead! - I wanted a word!

713
00:28:06,916 --> 00:28:08,125
Go ahead?

714
00:28:08,125 --> 00:28:10,958
I wanted to say that something happened, and - Stay well!

715
00:28:10,958 --> 00:28:13,500
I felt I should come see you in person. - Stay well!

716
00:28:13,500 --> 00:28:15,750
Move along, it’s nothing!

717
00:28:15,791 --> 00:28:17,083
Honestly, it’s nothing! (Crowd murmurs)

718
00:28:17,125 --> 00:28:19,166
A firecracker exploded in one of the kids’ hands, (Crowd murmurs)

719
00:28:19,208 --> 00:28:21,791
It’s nothing, no need to gather! (Crowd murmurs)

720
00:28:21,791 --> 00:28:22,791
Mr. Doctor…

721
00:28:22,833 --> 00:28:23,875
I…

722
00:28:23,916 --> 00:28:26,541
In all humility,

723
00:28:26,583 --> 00:28:28,250
I want to apologize to you.

724
00:28:29,458 --> 00:28:30,541
Last night,

725
00:28:30,541 --> 00:28:32,291
I was angry,

726
00:28:32,291 --> 00:28:34,250
I wasn’t feeling well.

727
00:28:34,291 --> 00:28:35,458
You know…

728
00:28:35,500 --> 00:28:38,583
When I get angry, my heart seizes up.

729
00:28:38,791 --> 00:28:41,250
Our health is in your hands.

730
00:28:41,250 --> 00:28:42,666
Please forgive us!

731
00:28:44,041 --> 00:28:46,041
Stay well.

732
00:28:47,708 --> 00:28:50,416
Stay well. - You showed great kindness. Thank you.

733
00:28:50,416 --> 00:28:52,875
Stay well. - Well, when a person gets angry…

734
00:28:53,500 --> 00:28:54,708
- Come, let’s go.

735
00:28:55,500 --> 00:28:58,666
♪ Bayat-e Tork piece – Morteza Mahjubi ♪

736
00:29:44,416 --> 00:29:45,666
Oh Agha Joon!

737
00:29:47,958 --> 00:29:48,666
Home!

738
00:29:52,791 --> 00:29:54,250
You go home too!

739
00:29:54,250 --> 00:29:55,916
Don’t let yourself be seen around here again.

740
00:29:57,791 --> 00:29:58,791
Feshfeshoo!

741
00:30:03,583 --> 00:30:04,500
Poori!

742
00:30:07,291 --> 00:30:08,458
dear uncle…

743
00:30:08,750 --> 00:30:10,625
Eh… bring that rifle home.

744
00:30:16,666 --> 00:30:19,166
(Sound of cart wheels)

745
00:30:36,666 --> 00:30:38,208
Help carry it to the end of the garden. - Shaajoon!

746
00:30:38,708 --> 00:30:40,083
Two by two.

747
00:30:40,083 --> 00:30:40,750
Shaajoon!

748
00:30:40,750 --> 00:30:42,208
What’s all this today? - Mind the door!

749
00:30:42,208 --> 00:30:43,625
How do I know! How do I know!

750
00:30:43,625 --> 00:30:44,916
Go ask him yourself!

751
00:30:44,916 --> 00:30:47,625
I suppose he wants to celebrate my death!

752
00:30:47,666 --> 00:30:48,750
How do I know! - No… there, there!

753
00:30:49,125 --> 00:30:49,541
There,

754
00:30:49,583 --> 00:30:50,541
Put it all the way back. - Agha Joon!

755
00:30:51,000 --> 00:30:52,125
What’s all this today?

756
00:30:52,125 --> 00:30:53,666
Where have you been until now? - In the alley.

757
00:30:53,708 --> 00:30:54,708
Go call the kids,

758
00:30:54,750 --> 00:30:56,208
Help arrange the chairs in the garden.

759
00:30:56,250 --> 00:30:57,291
Tonight’s a party!

760
00:30:57,291 --> 00:30:58,416
What celebration, Agha Joon?

761
00:30:58,416 --> 00:30:59,291
What celebration?

762
00:30:59,291 --> 00:31:00,458
Hello… hello…

763
00:31:00,500 --> 00:31:01,625
One, two, three!

764
00:31:01,666 --> 00:31:02,791
Can’t this get any louder?

765
00:31:02,791 --> 00:31:04,166
No, Sir, this is already too much!

766
00:31:04,166 --> 00:31:05,291
It’ll deafen people!

767
00:31:05,916 --> 00:31:08,750
(Testing the microphone)

768
00:31:08,750 --> 00:31:09,958
Tonight,

769
00:31:09,958 --> 00:31:12,375
Is the anniversary of my marriage with your mother.

770
00:31:12,458 --> 00:31:13,500
We’re holding a celebration.

771
00:31:14,125 --> 00:31:15,166
Wedding anniversary celebration,

772
00:31:15,166 --> 00:31:17,750
With this kind and united family.

773
00:31:17,875 --> 00:31:18,500
Tonight,

774
00:31:18,541 --> 00:31:19,666
Everyone is here!

775
00:31:19,666 --> 00:31:21,250
All the relatives… (The sound distorts)

776
00:31:21,291 --> 00:31:22,208
What’s wrong with it!

777
00:31:22,250 --> 00:31:23,333
Why did it do that! - What are you saying, Sir!

778
00:31:23,708 --> 00:31:25,708
It’s coming through the loudspeaker!

779
00:31:25,750 --> 00:31:26,458
Hello… hello!

780
00:31:26,875 --> 00:31:27,541
One, two, three…

781
00:31:27,583 --> 00:31:28,291
Hello! One, two…

782
00:31:28,333 --> 00:31:29,333
One, two, three, four…

783
00:31:29,375 --> 00:31:30,083
One, two, three, four…

784
00:31:30,125 --> 00:31:31,083
One… testing…

785
00:31:31,125 --> 00:31:31,916
One, two, three, four…

786
00:31:31,958 --> 00:31:33,458
One, two, three, one, one, two

787
00:31:33,500 --> 00:31:34,416
One, two…

788
00:31:34,458 --> 00:31:35,666
Oh man…

789
00:31:35,666 --> 00:31:36,416
Hello, hello!

790
00:31:36,458 --> 00:31:37,916
- It’s good now, Sir! - One…

791
00:31:39,000 --> 00:31:40,250
One… hello…

792
00:31:40,291 --> 00:31:42,000
Tonight we’re celebrating!

793
00:31:42,166 --> 00:31:44,500
Wedding anniversary celebration.

794
00:31:44,750 --> 00:31:45,833
Eh… by the way, let me see!

795
00:31:45,833 --> 00:31:48,208
Did you invite Shamsali and Asdollah Mirza?

796
00:31:48,333 --> 00:31:50,458
All the relatives must be invited!

797
00:31:50,625 --> 00:31:51,583
Hello…

798
00:31:51,833 --> 00:31:53,000
Hello… hello…

799
00:31:53,083 --> 00:31:54,000
Hello…

800
00:31:54,708 --> 00:31:55,250
Man,

801
00:31:55,291 --> 00:31:57,291
Do you even know what you’re doing?

802
00:31:57,333 --> 00:31:59,625
I want to tell beautiful stories to the guests.

803
00:31:59,666 --> 00:32:01,041
Music and singing.

804
00:32:01,750 --> 00:32:02,375
I want,

805
00:32:02,416 --> 00:32:04,541
To invite the singer Ghamar-ol-Moluk Vaziri,

806
00:32:04,541 --> 00:32:05,625
To come here,

807
00:32:05,625 --> 00:32:08,208
To sing for the guests in front of this loudspeaker.

808
00:32:08,208 --> 00:32:27,916
♪ Sound of singing ♪

809
00:32:27,916 --> 00:32:28,750
Ghasem!

810
00:32:29,083 --> 00:32:29,750
Sir!

811
00:32:29,750 --> 00:32:31,916
Sir, I beg you, help us!

812
00:32:31,958 --> 00:32:33,958
